---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="2026 Business Card Calendar"
  description="A full year calendar that fits on a business card — clever row alignment lets every month share the same date grid. Download as PDF or print in 3D."
>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem; }

  .hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e64b4 0%, #0d3a6e 100%);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 2.2rem 2rem;
    color: white;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(30,100,180,0.25);
  }
  .hero h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .hero p  { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; opacity: .9; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* card preview */
  .preview-wrap {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .card-frame {
    background: white;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.15), 0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.1);
    display: inline-block;
    max-width: 560px;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .card-frame img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .card-caption {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: .65rem;
    font-size: .82rem;
    color: #6b7280;
  }

  /* how-to */
  .how-to {
    background: #f0f7ff;
    border-left: 4px solid #1e64b4;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .dark .how-to { background: #0f1f38; border-color: #3b82f6; }
  .how-to h2 { margin: 0 0 .75rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: #1e64b4; }
  .dark .how-to h2 { color: #60a5fa; }
  .how-to ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.4rem; color: #1f2937; }
  .dark .how-to ol { color: #e5e7eb; }
  .how-to li { margin-bottom: .45rem; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .how-to .example {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid #d1e3f8;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: .6rem .9rem;
    margin-top: .85rem;
    font-size: .88rem;
    color: #374151;
  }
  .dark .how-to .example { background: #1e3a5f; border-color: #2d5a9e; color: #d1d5db; }
  .how-to .example strong { color: #1e64b4; }
  .dark .how-to .example strong { color: #93c5fd; }

  /* downloads */
  .downloads h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .dl-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .dl-card {
    border: 2px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.2rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color .2s, box-shadow .2s, transform .15s;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: .4rem;
  }
  .dl-card:hover {
    border-color: #1e64b4;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(30,100,180,.15);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .dark .dl-card { border-color: #374151; }
  .dark .dl-card:hover { border-color: #3b82f6; }
  .dl-icon { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .dl-title { font-weight: 600; font-size: .95rem; }
  .dl-desc { font-size: .8rem; color: #6b7280; }

  /* insight */
  .insight {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.05);
  }
  .dark .insight { background: #1f2937; border-color: #374151; }
  .insight h2 { margin: 0 0 .75rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .insight p  { margin: 0 0 .65rem; font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .insight p:last-child { margin: 0; }

  .stl-note {
    background: #fefce8;
    border: 1px solid #fde047;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: .88rem;
    color: #78350f;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .dark .stl-note { background: #1c1407; border-color: #78350f; color: #fde68a; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
  }
</style>

<div class="page">

  <div class="hero">
    <h1>2026 Business Card Calendar</h1>
    <p>
      A complete year on a 3.5&thinsp;&times;&thinsp;2&Prime; card — the clever trick:
      every month shares the same lower rows (8–14, 15–21&hellip;).
      Only the first week shifts, and the month key tells you exactly where to start.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Calendar preview -->
  <div class="preview-wrap">
    <div class="card-frame">
      <img src="/calendar/preview.png" alt="2026 Business Card Calendar" />
      <div class="card-caption">Actual business-card size (3.5&Prime; &times; 2&Prime;) — print and fold away.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- How to read it -->
  <div class="how-to">
    <h2>How to read it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Find your <strong>month</strong> in the right-hand column (e.g. <em>August → Sa</em>).</li>
      <li>Use the <strong>Sa row</strong> as the first week of that month — Saturday is the 1st.</li>
      <li>The rows <strong>8–14, 15–21, 22–28, 29–31</strong> are identical for every month; just continue downward.</li>
      <li>The footer shows how many days each month has, so you know where to stop.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="example">
      <strong>Example — August 2026 (Sa):</strong>
      week 1 is the "Sa" row → Aug 1 = Sat, Aug 2 = Sun&hellip; Aug 7 = Fri.
      Then Aug 8 = Sat, Aug 9 = Sun&hellip; Aug 31 = Mon.
      Check footer: A31 ✓
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Downloads -->
  <div class="downloads">
    <h2>Downloads</h2>
    <div class="dl-grid">
      <a class="dl-card" href="/calendar/calendar-2026.pdf" download>
        <span class="dl-icon">📄</span>
        <span class="dl-title">PDF</span>
        <span class="dl-desc">Print-ready business card — exact 3.5&Prime;&thinsp;&times;&thinsp;2&Prime; page size.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="dl-card" href="/calendar/calendar-2026.stl" download>
        <span class="dl-icon">🖨️</span>
        <span class="dl-title">STL (3D print)</span>
        <span class="dl-desc">Business card with raised text geometry, ready for your slicer.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="dl-card" href="/calendar/calendar-2026.tex" download>
        <span class="dl-icon">📝</span>
        <span class="dl-title">LaTeX source</span>
        <span class="dl-desc">Full .tex source — tweak colors, font, year, or layout.</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STL note -->
  <div class="stl-note">
    <strong>3D printing tips:</strong>
    Best detail on a resin printer (0.05&thinsp;mm layer height).
    For FDM, scale to <strong>150%</strong> in your slicer to widen the smallest strokes above 0.4&thinsp;mm.
    No supports needed — flat base sits directly on the bed.
  </div>

  <!-- Design insight -->
  <div class="insight">
    <h2>The alignment trick</h2>
    <p>
      A standard monthly calendar repeats four or five rows of dates (the "weeks 2–5" rows:
      8–14, 15–21, 22–28, 29–31) <em>identically</em> every month — only the first row changes
      based on which day of the week the 1st falls on. There are only seven possible first rows,
      so the entire year can be encoded as one universal grid plus a seven-entry lookup.
    </p>
    <p>
      Months with fewer days simply stop early — the footer
      <code>F&thinsp;28 A&thinsp;30&hellip;</code> tells you where each month ends.
      Two months sharing the same start-day key (e.g. <em>Jan&thinsp;&amp;&thinsp;Oct</em>
      both start on Thursday in 2026) are fully identical calendars — a fact hidden in
      plain sight that this card makes instantly visible.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>
</Layout>
